{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5dde3370-f06f-4e14-96ca-33634b26a34e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"An authorization audit was performed on the API, identifying an authorization flaw allowing users to alter private tasks belonging to other users.\n\n### Summary of Findings\n- **Can one user see or change what they shouldn't?**\n  **Yes.** While private task contents were protected from read, edit, delete, and comments, unauthorized users could still mutate metadata on other users' private tasks:\n  1. `POST /tasks/{id}/like`: Allowed any authenticated user to like another user's private task and increment its like count.\n  2. `POST /tasks/{id}/view`: Allowed any authenticated user to register views on another user's private task and increment its view count.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n1. In [`api.py`](file:///tmp/h-LmDA3R/api.py#L163-L172), added `can_access(user, task)` authorization checks on both `like` and `view` actions, returning `403 Forbidden` if the caller does not own the private task.\n2. In [`tests/test_api.py`](file:///tmp/h-LmDA3R/tests/test_api.py#L71-L106), added comprehensive multi-user authorization regression tests covering all private task actions.\n3. Created [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-LmDA3R/ANSWER.md) detailing the findings, endpoint analysis, and remediation.\n","duration_seconds":95.291335,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":133706,"output_tokens":8008,"thinking_tokens":5166,"cache_read_tokens":210110,"total_tokens":141714}}}
